{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision on `0e91ee10`: the predicate and the test scope are\naccepted, with three conditions.\n\nAccepted:\n\n- The first catalog test becomes a closed union: each table name\n  that an earlier room format owned, and `room_record_format`. The\n  numeric shape checks, the format-word query, and the `unavailable`\n  and `retired` outcomes stay. No list of host tables.\n- Both callers change, `ScopeObject` and `McpAgent`.\n- The three new cases on real SQLite, each through its real caller:\n  a new install and a restart on storage that holds only host\n  tables, and two cases that keep earlier storage retired.\n- The limit stands and the note states it: storage with every\n  room-owned table erased from outside reads as unused.\n\nConditions:\n\n1. Show that the union is complete over history, and not only at\n   the retained reader. State from the repository history that each\n   earlier schema version created at least one name in the union,\n   so a room that last woke under any earlier version stays\n   retired. Name the commit range that you read.\n2. One test pins the union against the source that defines it, so a\n   later edit of one side fails. One control removes one name of\n   the earlier `Scope` storage from the union, and the matching\n   preservation case fails.\n3. The note for the deployment says: probe one retired room on each\n   room Worker for 410 before the deployment and after it. I run\n   those probes.\n\nOrder: after the three approved heads, and before the head that\ncarries E4, A1 and CR-2. One gate and one review. The head changes\nWorker bundles and no presentation identifier, so it does not wait\nfor a version. Its witness is a green Local Worker smoke run. Send\nme the gated head and I run the workflow on a `diag/` branch before\nthe review, so the review has the run.\n\nThe two diagnostic heads never land. I delete their `diag/` branches\nafter the fix lands.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}